# Nursing (Ward) Patient Flow

## 0. Overview

This file is the direct Nursing flow source of truth for HOSSPI HMS. Ward nursing is anchored to the **IPD admission / encounter**. Nursing executes vitals, observations, MAR, care tasks, handovers, and discharge nursing clearance â" without owning admission lifecycle, ICU stays, or final discharge closure. Align with [`.cursor/flows/ipd-flow.mdc`](./ipd-flow.mdc), [`.cursor/flows/opd-flow.mdc`](./opd-flow.mdc), [`.cursor/flows/icu-flow.mdc`](./icu-flow.mdc), [`.cursor/flows/discharge-flow.mdc`](./discharge-flow.mdc), [`.cursor/flows/pharmacy-flow.mdc`](./pharmacy-flow.mdc), and [`.cursor/app-write-up.mdc`](../app-write-up.mdc).

## 1. Goal

Enable ward nurses, charge nurses, and nursing supervisors to run inpatient nursing care: admission checklist, vitals, MAR, nursing notes, handovers, transfer support, ICU escalation handoff, and discharge nursing clearance â" on a calm, scannable workspace.

### Central encounter rule

The **IPD admission** is the parent record. Nursing notes, vitals, medication administration, care plans, and handovers attach to that admission. OPD vitals during outpatient stages attach to the **OPD encounter** only â" do not duplicate encounters.

